How do low stratus clouds and high cirrus clouds differ in their dominant global radiative impact?
#pagebreak()
#set page(width: a_width, height: auto, margin: a_margin)
#set text(size: a_size)
Low stratus cool (albedo dominates); high cirrus warm (greenhouse longwave trapping dominates)
#pagebreak()
#set page(width: a_width, height: auto, margin: a_margin)
#set text(size: a_size)
Low stratus warm the surface; high cirrus cool the surface
#pagebreak()
#set page(width: a_width, height: auto, margin: a_margin)
#set text(size: a_size)
Both cloud types exert identical net warming effects regardless of altitude
#pagebreak()
#set page(width: a_width, height: auto, margin: a_margin)
#set text(size: a_size)
Clouds exert zero net radiative effect on the planetary energy budget
